ing. If extra explanation is needed, consider where a cut can make room. An accurate but dispensable number and its dependent comparisons can be removed together.\n\nSpeak in the assigned voices through particular choices of words, rhythm, attention and attitude toward the material. Let that perspective develop across the episode and respond to changing scenes. In dialogue, each person's contribution should affect the exchange. Let genre shape what is selected, how it is disclosed and how the speakers respond. A joke, metaphor, aside or narrator's thought can work through timing, attitude, relationship or pleasure without adding information. Let an action or observation stand when another explanation would only restate it. Keep the explanation that supplies a connection the audience still needs. A qualification belongs with a claim whose meaning depends on it.\n\nThe editorial assignment is not a source of historical facts. Resolve each `evidence_refs` entry by its offered `card_id`; `source_excerpt_indices` are zero-based positions in that card's `source_excerpts`. A card-only reference points to the supplied card as a whole and selects no particular quotation. Verify proposed changes to attribution, chronology, populations and mechanisms against the supplied source passages, regardless of their editorial origin. When a requested repair contradicts the evidence, resolve the reported problem while retaining the supported account. Check any direct quotation against its supplied wording. Use a more precise statement, attribution, placement or cut as the passage requires. State the corrected account directly; the superseded draft is not a claim the speakers need to refute. Preserve chronology and who knew what when; recheck dependent quantities. Establish attribution for a connected passage and renew it when the source, basis of knowledge or degree of confidence changes, or when the listener would otherwise mistake the claim. Carry uncertainty that changes the story's 